            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Baidu chip unit files for IPO, Trump delays furniture tariff hike",
            "description": "<p>Yahoo Finance executive editor <a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://www.yahoo.com/author/brian-sozzi/\">Brian Sozzi</a> tracks several of the day's top trending stock tickers, including Tesla (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/TSLA\">TSLA</a>) reporting that both its EV deliveries for the fourth quarter and full-year 2025 fell just short of expectations, Baidu (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/BIDU\">BIDU</a>, <a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/9888.HK\">9888.HK</a>) stock jumping on its chip business filing for an IPO in Hong Kong, and furniture companies Wayfair (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/W\">W</a>) and RH (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:6;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/RH\">RH</a>) getting a shares boost as President Trump rolls back his tariff hike on furniture imports.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more\u00a0<a data-i13n=\"cpos:7;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/opening-bid/\">Opening Bid</a>.</p>",
